      "content": "The idea of trying to explain yourself when you feel so depleted is exhausting, and that feeling of futility is completely valid. It is a massive effort to maintain a facade when you're running on empty, and that effort itself is draining. Instead of thinking about \"fixing\" something, perhaps just focusing on making the next small moment a little less heavy could be a starting point. Reaching out to a crisis line can be a place where you don't have to \"fix\" anything, just let the weight out.",
